From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:07:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] BitstreamConverter: compare the end of sequence as an hevc
 nal

The end of sequence check compares the hevc nal type with the avc value,
so it never matches. At a clip end the base layer's last packet ends in
end of sequence, ahead of the enhancement layer and rpu. The decoder
stops there and outputs the last picture without dovi metadata, so the
output switches to hdr10 for that frame.
---
 xbmc/utils/BitstreamConverter.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/BitstreamConverter.cpp b/xbmc/utils/BitstreamConverter.cpp
--- a/xbmc/utils/BitstreamConverter.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/utils/BitstreamConverter.cpp
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
       buf += 4;
       nal_type = (buf[0] >> 1) & 0x3f;
 
-      if (nal_type != AVC_NAL_END_SEQUENCE)
+      if (nal_type != HEVC_NAL_EOS_NUT || end - (buf + size) > 4)
         BitstreamAllocAndCopy(&m_convertBuffer, &offset, buf, size, nal_type);
       else
       {
